# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# setup: report
# board: dead
# dead-after: 8
# A mounted board that stops answering costs the loop nothing.
#
# The worst freeze in the tree: every 400 ms the desk asks each mounted
# board what changed, with a four-second ceiling -- and a board that has
# gone quiet costs the whole four, every 400 ms, on the one thread that
# draws and takes clicks.  Here the board is real and answers until the
# eighth second; from then on nothing comes back.  What is asserted is
# the longest turn the loop took, read from the watchdog: a number that
# was four thousand before the wire left the loop.
wait 60
expect-read trail:mount /devices/tiku
expect-under turns 100
note the board goes quiet now; ten notice pumps later, the loop is asked
wait 1400
expect-under turns 100
note and the desk is still here, answering, its mount still standing
report
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_reports/latest-report.txt /devices/tiku
quit
